		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη,</span>
		ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>state of being attacked on both sides,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιβολίῃ ἔχεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.74
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>ambiguity,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1461a25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SE</u>
				165b26
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
